review_comments.body:
Why not take advantage of the stored size up front?

```
  std::size_t escape_size = static_cast<std::size_t>(escape[7]);
  if (JSON_HEDLEY_UNLIKELY(write_buffer.size() - write_buffer_pos < escape_size))
```

This allows you to put more bytes into the buffer without flushing, and copies fewer bytes.

